      <version name="1.2.1" author="Quaz (EON Studios)" time="2026-09-29T21:41:21Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[GainKit 2.5.0. The name sits on top of the mixer strip in every view (the VU over the knob, the knob alone, the VU alone): as a plain row, on a band in the track's colour, or not at all (THEME panel: NAME). The VU alone gets its own STEREO / MONO key under the name, shows the gain as a tint of the meter's face (up from the middle for a boost, down for a cut), and prints the value under the meter while you set it or all the time (THEME panel: VALUE). The meter can take the track's colour, in the strip and in the window (THEME panel: VU COLOR). The name is the one typed on the meter or the track's, and the colour the track's, from the GainKit Plus script. DDC: 2x now oversamples only the detector, so it follows the peaks between samples while the audio stays at the project's rate: 2x keeps the top end (it used to take about 2 to 3 dB off at 15 kHz and 5 to 6 dB at 20 kHz) and adds no latency, and with 2x off DDC sounds exactly as before. Its gain-reduction meter is updated once per block instead of on every sample. De-Esser: the Target and Monitor switches take effect between audio blocks. The meter and the switches change no sound.]]></changelog>
